Hand-written intro: testing is sacred.

<!-- strata:hub:begin — GENERATED, do not edit below -->
## pytest  (4)
- [[pytest-fixture-teardown]] — Session-scoped DB fixtures leak connections unless torn down; tests then hang at exit.
- [[pytest-markers-registered]] — Every custom pytest marker is declared in pyproject.toml; unknown markers fail the run.
- [[pytest-parallel-xdist]] — Use pytest -n auto with per-worker database names to parallelize the integration suite.
- [[test-database-per-worker]] — The test harness creates app_test_gw0..gwN databases so parallel workers never share state.

## ci  (3)
- [[ci-pipeline-stages]] — The CI pipeline has four ordered stages; integration only runs after lint and unit tests pass.
- [[coverage-floor]] — Line coverage for the app package must not drop below 85 percent; CI enforces the floor.
- [[flaky-test-quarantine]] — Flaky tests are marked quarantine and tracked; automatic retries are not allowed in CI.

## debugging  (2)
- [[hanging-test-diagnosis]] — Dump thread stacks with py-spy to see which non-daemon thread keeps a finished suite alive.
- [[snapshot-test-updates]] — Syrupy snapshots are refreshed by running pytest with --snapshot-update and reviewing the diff.

